<title>PORTUGAL: PORTUGAL'S NON-EU TRADE DEFICIT UP YR/YR IN JUNE.</title>
<headline>PORTUGAL'S NON-EU TRADE DEFICIT UP YR/YR IN JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's trade deficit with non-European Union countries rose to 46.4 billion escudos in June from 40.1 billion in the same 1996 month, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In the first six months of the year, the accumulated deficit rose 13 percent to 335.1 billion escudos.</p>
<p>In billions of escudos:</p>
<p>		  June 97  May 97  June 96  Jan-June 97 Jan-June 96</p>
<p> Imports	 117.5   116.7    93.5	709.3	 658.7</p>
<p> Exports	  71.1    63.7    53.4	374.2	 362.2</p>
<p> Deficit	  46.4    53.0    40.1	335.1	 296.5</p>
<p>Note - 1997 figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>($1=188 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
